### Vertex Position Detector

The Vertex Position Detector (VPD) is a position detector fully integrated into STAR trigger system. It provides input to the MB trigger. The VPD consist of two detector assemblies, one on the east and one on the west of STAR. These two assemblies are consist of 19 detectors composed of a Pb converter followed by a fast, plastic scintillator which is read out by a photomultiplier tube. A schematic view and photograph of a VPD assembly is shown in Fig. 55 and a side view of the detector is shown in Fig. 56.

Two VPD detectors provide the start time for time-of-flight measurement in TOF detector. The information from the detector is used both in the STAR Level-0 trigger and offline to measure the location of the primary collision vertex along the beam pipe (Vz).

